---
extras: ["nocull"]
title: Placing the exit
---
Put the exit near a point you choose, or let a Dijkstra map find the tile that is farthest from the start [[t:244-250 s:26 s:27]].

## The rule
```text
right:    the exit is the open tile nearest the middle of the right edge
farthest: flood outward from the start, counting steps;
          the exit is the reachable tile with the highest count
then find the route from the start to the exit
```

The talk calls the second the least accessible part of the map, for when you really dislike your player [[t:249-250]]. With a start in the middle it calls putting the exit there a really bad idea, and a great way to hide something [[t:249-256]].

## Step through it
@@steps limit=4

## Controls
@@control at
`right` takes the open tile nearest the middle of the right edge [[c18:92-109 g]]. `farthest` takes the tile with the largest walking distance from the start [[c19:92-101]].

## What it produces, measured
@@measured

From the left edge to the right, the route is {{c18.path.median}} steps at the median. From the center to the farthest tile it is {{c19.path.median}} [[run:c18.path.median c19.path.median]]. The least accessible exit is the nearer one here, because a start in the middle has less map on any side of it [[own]].

## Where it fails
@@fails

Take the cull out and it does fail. In a recipe of our own, the same pipeline without its cull, the exit lands in a cave the start can’t reach on {{nocull.fails.exit-unreachable}} of 200 seeds [[run:nocull.fails.exit-unreachable]]. [Seed 0]({{recipe:nocull}}) is one.

